WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.770
-Everybody, Madonna is here!
Madonna!

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:08.408
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:10.443
I was trying to think of
a question to ask you

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.111
that's never been asked.

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:14.614
-Good luck.
-I know.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.049
How about this one?
Ready for this?

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.183
-Yeah.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.651
-This might be the best question
I've ever asked.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:19.986
-Okay.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:22.222
-Has any review of anything

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:25.025
you've done gotten it right?

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:31.263
Is that a good question?
-I mean, occasionally.

00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:33.232
It's rare.
-So they don't, really.

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:35.334
-In the 40 years that I've been
doing what I've been doing --

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.169
-40 years?
-40 years. Can you believe it?

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:39.138
-No. That's insane.
-It is. Yeah.

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:42.574
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.574 --> 00:00:44.778
-Do you know who you are?
Do you even know who you are?

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:45.778
You are Madonna. Oh, my God.

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:46.946
-I still don't even know
who I am.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:49.648
-Yeah, you really are
unbelievable.

00:00:49.648 --> 00:00:51.684
I mean, the first single was
what? "Everybody?"

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:52.818
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:54.787
-And do you remember
anything about that?

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.589
Like, what would you do to --
Do you remember

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:59.192
hearing yourself on the radio,
and going, "Wow"?

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.460
-I remember I was living on
the Upper West Side,

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.166
on 99th and Riverside Drive,
and was just broke

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:10.703
and wondering if things were
ever going to work out for me.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.272
And I had signed my record deal.

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:15.742
And I was told that they
were going to start

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.444
playing my song on the radio,
"Everybody."

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:18.711
-Yeah.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:23.315
-And then, suddenly,
my roommate had her radio on

00:01:23.315 --> 00:01:26.686
down the hall, and I heard it
drifting down the hallway.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.421
And I was like,
"Wait, what is that?

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.522
What is that?"

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:30.857
And I ran down the hall,
and she's like,

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:33.626
"They're playing
your song on the radio.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:37.063
And I just stood there
like, "Wow!

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.765
It happened. It works."

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:41.367
It was like magic.
-Yeah.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.902
-It was the most amazing moment.

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.304
-Is this going to be in this --
I heard there's a rumor that --

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:47.040
-A visual autobiography?

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.375
-Yes, of course.
-Don't call it a biopic.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:52.078
-But, yeah, -- I would never
call it a biopic.

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:55.481
-How dare you?
-No, how dare you?

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:58.518
I think it's cool.
Once again, no one's done this.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:01.353
-Well, the reason I'm doing it
is because a bunch of people

00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:05.891
have tried to write movies about
me, but they're always men.

00:02:05.891 --> 00:02:07.593
Ugh!

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:10.529
-Wait. What do you mean?
What are you talking about?

00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:12.398
[ Cheers and applause ]
No.

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.033
Men are good.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.134
Some men.
-Some men are good.

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:16.402
-Yeah.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:20.540
-Men -- "Good men" is pretty
much an oxymoron, but --

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.675
-Oh, my gosh.
-Anyways...

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.076
No, because people
were writing --

00:02:24.076 --> 00:02:26.880
I read Universal was doing a --

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.148
Like, they sent me the script
because they wanted my blessing.

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:30.883
And I read it,
and it was the most hideous,

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:33.252
superficial crap I ever read.

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:36.956
And then I found out that
some -- I found out --

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.891
I'm not even going to
say his name,

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:41.494
but he's a total misogynist --
was directing.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.363
And I'm thinking,
"Why would these people

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:44.864
make a movie about my life?"

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.766
There's nothing true
in the script.

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.568
The guy who is making it
has no understanding of women,

00:02:49.568 --> 00:02:52.238
no appreciation of women,
no respect for women.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.707
So, like, this happened
a couple of times,

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.410
and I had to, like,
call people up,

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.279
call up the heads of studios,

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:01.680
call up my agents and
threaten them

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.383
and say that I will, like,
stand in front of the building

00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:08.387
and make -- and protest
and make everybody's life

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:10.356
a misery if
they go through with it.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.959
And they still did not
take me seriously.

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:17.030
-So, finally, I just threw
down the gauntlet.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.166
Have you ever thrown down
the gauntlet?

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:23.035
-I've thought about it.

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:24.103
-Therein lies the rub.

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.105
You have to throw down
the gauntlet.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.708
-"Therein lies the rub."
Yeah, I did.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.743
-You have to do this.
You have to do this.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.712
-Oh, look at this.

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.747
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:40.186
-Okay? Never mind.
I'll pick it up myself.

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.355
-Yeah, exactly.
"I'll pick it up myself."

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.089
-Because that's what
you've got to do in life.

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:45.658
You've got to
pick it up yourself.

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:47.326
Anyways, no, I just said,
"You know what?

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:51.197
There's nobody on this planet
that can write or direct

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:54.600
and make a movie about me
better than me."

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.235
And that is just the truth.

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:58.237
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I agree.

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:00.139
I love that you're doing that.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.908
And, honestly, no one has -- -

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.342
-Keep talking while
I undo my glove.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:06.045
-Yeah, no problem. Yeah.
-Say interesting things, please.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.814
-I have an
interesting thing to say.

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:09.682
These are myths and rumors
about you,

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:10.716
and I want to know
if some things

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:12.017
are true and
some things are false.

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:13.719
Do you mind me going through
these and you tell me?

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:17.123
-Go ahead.
-Well, do I believe you?

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.324
Will you tell me the truth?

00:04:19.324 --> 00:04:21.827
[ Laughs ]

00:04:21.827 --> 00:04:24.563
Honestly, I can't even tell you
how nervous I feel right now.

00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:28.701
You just -- You do -- You make
me so -- you make me so --

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:31.470
-♪ Good inside ♪

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.539
-Yeah, you really do.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:36.709
Okay.
-Come on, you guys. Like a...

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.544
-♪ Virgin ♪

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:40.680
-Oh, my God.
-♪ Touched for the... ♪

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:43.082
-♪ Very first time ♪

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:47.720
-♪ Like a...♪
-♪ Virgin ♪

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.289
-♪ When your heart beats ♪

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.992
♪ Next to mine ♪

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:55.227
-Come on, now.
That's what -- Look at this.

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:57.029
[ Cheers and applause ]
An impromptu...

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:58.197
That's what I'm talking about.

00:05:00.699 --> 00:05:02.935
Alright. Wait, wait, wait!
-Trying to get my --

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:04.036
-Alright, ready?

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:05.237
These are myths
and rumors about you,

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:07.206
and it may or may not be true.

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:09.808
Your first job was at
Dunkin' Donuts

00:05:09.808 --> 00:05:11.477
and you were fired.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:15.181
-Yeah.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.249
It was one of the first jobs
I had working

00:05:17.249 --> 00:05:18.317
when I moved to Manhattan.

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:19.852
And I did get fired
because I was

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:21.721
playing with the jelly squirter.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:24.289
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.289 --> 00:05:25.324
-Okay, alright.

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:26.759
-Have you ever seen
a jelly squirter?

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.594
-No, no, no, I haven't.
Alright, here we go.

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:30.063
Alright.
♪♪

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:32.999
No, stop, stop, stop.
Okay, here we go.

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:34.934
Just stop, stop, stop.
Alright, here we go.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.836
-It's funny how everything
is a sexual innuendo.

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.938
-It really is. How about this?

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:42.041
"Vogue" was originally only
going to be a B-side

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.376
because it wasn't considered
strong enough

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:45.445
to be released as a single.

00:05:45.445 --> 00:05:47.080
-Yeah, it's true.
-What?

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.248
But "Vogue" is
the biggest song ever.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:50.683
It was the B-side?
What was the A-side?

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.151
-Well, there's a lot of
unenlightened people

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:53.185
in the world.

00:05:53.185 --> 00:05:56.355
-Yeah.
-They can't see into the future.

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:59.225
-Did you write "Jimmy Jimmy"
thinking of me?

00:06:00.859 --> 00:06:02.295
-Nope.
-Okay.

00:06:05.564 --> 00:06:07.433
-Here's a myth or a rumor.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.934
You turned down
the role of Catwoman

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:10.135
in the film "Batman Returns,"

00:06:10.135 --> 00:06:12.538
and the lead in "Showgirls"
you turned down.

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:15.975
Did you ever see those movies?
And what did you think of them?

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:19.345
-I saw them both.

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:22.115
And I was -- I regret that I
turned down Catwoman.

00:06:22.115 --> 00:06:23.649
That was pretty fierce.
-Oh, really?

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.251
-"Showgirls," no.

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:28.354
But I also turned down the role
in "The Matrix."

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:29.688
Can you believe that?
-You did?

00:06:29.688 --> 00:06:32.658
-I wanted to kill myself.
-Oh, stop it. You're Madonna.

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:35.093
-That's like one
the best movies ever made.

00:06:35.093 --> 00:06:36.995
-You don't regret anything.
Look at you.

00:06:36.995 --> 00:06:39.198
-A teeny, tiny part
of me regrets

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:41.734
that just one moment in my life.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:44.703
-Madonna, are...

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:46.472
Wow. You're unbelievable.

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:48.074
Why? Why?

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:49.842
But why are you such a
troublemaker?

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:51.243
Why? Just stop.
-Because.

00:06:51.243 --> 00:06:54.479
Because artists are just here
to disturb the peace.

00:06:54.479 --> 00:06:57.816
-Just stop. Just be good.

00:06:57.816 --> 00:07:00.820
-Okay, okay. I'm sorry.
-Behave!

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:02.255
-I will.
-Please behave!

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:03.723
-Okay!

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:06.492
-Madonna, I can't even tell
you -- I really do mean this.

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:09.761
I'm just -- I love you, and I'm
honored to have you here.

00:07:09.761 --> 00:07:12.098
And I just love you.
You're one in a million.

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:13.598
You're the best.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:13.598 --> 00:07:17.370
Madonna, "Madame X" is available
on Paramount+ tomorrow.

